   "documentation": "M_DISPATCH - one-transaction M/UM coil scan + acknowledge.\n   Replaces the Eckelmann MFKT strobe/quitt handshake (M_BEARBEITUNG_FB):\n   reads the whole RoboCNC M-coil window with a single FC1, pulses one BOOL\n   output per implemented M-code, and (AUTO_ACK) clears each seen coil with\n   FC5 - releasing a blocking M<n> exactly like the original immediate quitt.\n   UM<n> coils are already released by the read itself (:5008 read-detect\n   hook); the FC5 just clears the latch.\n   UNKNOWN_M reports the lowest set coil that is NOT in the implemented set\n   (original raised error 303); it too is acked to avoid deadlocking the\n   .din. Coils scanned: 0..1023.\n   M450/M500 (pneumatic second Z stage) are NOT auto-acked while HOLD450/\n   HOLD500 are TRUE: the caller acks them via MRESET when the stage limit\n   switch confirms - the RoboCNC-native replacement for Eckelmann's G152\n   block-until-in-position (a no-op in current firmware).\n   EN is the implicit IEC 61131-3 enable pin (STruC++ gates the body on it and\n   never assigns a declared EN member) -- do not re-test EN."
  },
